{
 "flograph_version": "0.1.31",
 "schema": 1,
 "graph": {
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "t41_intro",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     0,
     -320
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "# Files\n**Write Excel (Sheets)** puts several tables in one workbook, a sheet each;\n**File Operations** then copies it into an archive folder, zips the copy,\nand shows what a delete *would* remove (dry run). Everything goes in the\nfolder named by `out_dir` in **Variables**, relative to where flograph was\nstarted — change it there.",
     "width": 1100,
     "height": 200
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_vars",
    "type": "flograph.util.variables",
    "pos": [
     0,
     0
    ],
    "params": {
     "assignments": "out_dir = flograph_files_demo"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_sales",
    "type": "flograph.io.table",
    "pos": [
     0,
     160
    ],
    "params": {
     "data": "{\"version\": 2, \"columns\": [{\"name\": \"month\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"name\": \"revenue\", \"type\": \"number\"}], \"rows\": [[\"2026-07\", 23800], [\"2026-08\", 24600], [\"2026-09\", 26100]]}",
     "width": 300,
     "height": 180
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Sales"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_costs",
    "type": "flograph.io.table",
    "pos": [
     0,
     420
    ],
    "params": {
     "data": "{\"version\": 2, \"columns\": [{\"name\": \"month\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"name\": \"cost\", \"type\": \"number\"}], \"rows\": [[\"2026-07\", 17100], [\"2026-08\", 16900], [\"2026-09\", 18200]]}",
     "width": 300,
     "height": 180
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Costs"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_regions",
    "type": "flograph.io.table",
    "pos": [
     0,
     680
    ],
    "params": {
     "data": "{\"version\": 2, \"columns\": [{\"name\": \"region\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"name\": \"share\", \"type\": \"number\"}], \"rows\": [[\"North\", 0.42], [\"South\", 0.33], [\"East\", 0.25]]}",
     "width": 300,
     "height": 180
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Regions"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_xlsx",
    "type": "flograph.io.write_excel_sheets",
    "pos": [
     560,
     420
    ],
    "params": {
     "path": "${out_dir}/q3_pack.xlsx",
     "add_summary": true,
     "sheet_names": "Sales\nCosts\nBy region"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null,
    "extra_inputs": [
     {
      "name": "in3",
      "type": "dataframe"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_copy",
    "type": "flograph.automation.file_operations",
    "pos": [
     800,
     420
    ],
    "params": {
     "operation": "copy",
     "destination": "${out_dir}/archive/",
     "overwrite": true
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Copy to archive"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_zip",
    "type": "flograph.automation.file_operations",
    "pos": [
     1040,
     420
    ],
    "params": {
     "operation": "zip",
     "destination": "${out_dir}/archive.zip",
     "overwrite": true
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Zip the archive"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_dry",
    "type": "flograph.automation.file_operations",
    "pos": [
     1280,
     420
    ],
    "params": {
     "operation": "delete",
     "source": "${out_dir}/*.xlsx",
     "dry_run": true
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Delete (dry run)"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41_n_files",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     560,
     600
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "Each step hands its result on: the workbook's **path** → copied → the copy's\n**paths** → zipped. The delete is a **dry run**: its log lists what it would\nremove and nothing goes. The dashed wire is an *order edge* — it runs after\nthe zip, though no value passes.",
     "width": 760,
     "height": 160
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   }
  ],
  "connections": [
